// data-layer-serverplan-quality in Rerail logic: the main file, with the policy, its forbid clause `strategy-file-size`
// and the relational clauses quality-contracts-2, quality-contracts-3, quality-local-taxonomy and
// quality-project-taxonomy. The relational clauses quality-contracts-1 and quality-conditional-1 are part files:
// serverplan_quality.quality_contracts_1.rdl and serverplan_quality.quality_conditional_1.rdl.
// Source: gate/data-layer/packs/data-layer/candidates/rules/data-layer-serverplan-quality.json.
//
// Options at their defaults (entryPoint "all", oracleAnalyzer false). The inputs' matchers are verbatim, their `$option`
// nodes included (resolved at the defaults by the matcher compiler); stage SQL is read at the defaults.
// One relation per SQL stage, under the stage's name, prefixed c2_/c3_ (quality-contracts-2/-3 share stage names).
// The syntax table `nodes` is the tape of a document the clause's syntax_gate matched, less its excludeKinds; `parent`
// is `child`; `X_id`/`X_source` are `field` and `text` (a definition's name and body and an attribute's attribute are
// never NULL under `syntax: valid`); `ownership.fn`/`.cls` are not read. `import_descendants` (reachability over the
// syntax tree) is the root itself or a node `@within` it: no recursion. Stage columns no later stage reads are left out.
//
// Builtins: @rx_matches, @rx_extract, @substr, @within (tape: strict descendant). A builtin with no value (SQL NULL)
// binds nothing.
// strategy-file-size: a `regex` forbid on file.content (not an `ast` matcher), so the generated forbid block is empty;
// its rule is by hand, the "all" case of its `$option`.
// file_content(d, s): the document's whole source (W's file.content), core's `source` span's text (the module node's
// text starts at its first token, which would shift the line count by leading blank lines).
// findings layer (§8): strategy-file-size's anchor is capture.OVERFLOW (the 1501st line), which is no node: here the
// violation is at the document's module node.
// findings layer (§8): path/start_byte/end_byte are the node's; detector and identity (n.id, the keyword of a
// CompiledStep call, a taxonomy candidate's __start) are the findings layer's: rows collapse to one finding per (issue, node).
// ties: c3_ordered_occurrences (row_number by __start, __end DESC): two attributes never share a span, so none.
// OUTSIDE: none. LIMIT/choice: c3_ordered_occurrences' class_name/function_name (smallest enclosing class/function,
// LIMIT 1) is the nearest ancestor: unique.
